---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/main.astro";
import Header from "@/components/header.astro";
import TestCard from "@/components/test-card.astro";
---

<PageLayout title="Dual Stack Scenario Runner Laboratory" backgroundOpacity={0.4}>
  <Header titleLine1="Dual Stack Scenario Runner " titleLine2="Laboratory">
  </Header>

  <div class="mt-20 grid gap-6 items-start lg:grid-cols-2">
    <TestCard
      title="Historical Evidence Explorer"
      href="/evidence"
      actionText="Explore campaign evidence"
    >
      <span class="text-black">
      Interactive offline inspection of the October 2026 Happy Eyeballs experimental
      campaign (<code>ps028-a10-live-20261030-01</code>). Replay 280 valid live trials,
      compare scenario timing (S0–S6), inspect 765 connection attempts, and explore
      28,330 synchronized timeline events with full SHA-256 provenance.
      </span>
    </TestCard>

    <TestCard
      title="Scenario Analytics Dashboard"
      href="/analytics"
      actionText="View interactive analytics & PDF reports"
    >
      <span class="text-black">
      Interactive analytical dashboard and comparative visualizations across controlled
      network scenarios (S0–S6) and browser implementations (Chrome & Firefox).
      Inspect latency distributions, DNS timings, winner ratios, and download customized
      technical PDF reports.
      </span>
    </TestCard>

    <TestCard
      title="Connection Attempt Delay Test"
      href="tests/connection-attempt-delay"
    >
      <span class="text-black">
      Happy Eyeballs version 1 defines the racing of IPv4 vs. IPv6. The term
      Connection Attempt Delay (CAD) describes the delay a client waits for the
      IPv6 response before issuing an IPv4 connection. We test this behavior of
      your client by artificially adding latency to IPv6 packets. Depending on
      your client's settings, it will wait for the IPv6 connection attempt.
      </span>
    </TestCard>

  </div>
</PageLayout>
